<LegalLayout title="Privacy Policy" updated="9 August 2026">
  <h2>Who we are</h2>
  <p>
    M3 (“M3”, “we”, “us”) is a program from the team behind the AI Security
    Bootcamp, run as a collaboration between Constellation, Kairos and AISB and
    fiscally sponsored by Constellation Institute. This policy explains what
    personal information we collect through this website (m3fellowship.com) and
    our application and program processes, how we use it, and who we share it
    with.
  </p>
  <p>
    Because M3 operates under Constellation Institute's fiscal sponsorship, we
    might share your information with Constellation Institute, and
    <a href="https://constellation.org/privacy">Constellation Institute's Privacy Policy</a>
    also applies to its processing of your information.
  </p>

  <h2>Information we collect</h2>
  <p>
    We collect personal information when you interact with us, for example when
    you visit our website, apply to or take part in a program, sign up to hear
    from us, communicate with us by email, messaging and chat platforms, or
    video and phone calls, take part in interviews, surveys, or events, or
    otherwise engage with M3, whether online or in person. This includes:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Information you provide.</strong> Information you choose to share
      with us through these interactions, such as your contact details and any
      other information you give us as part of your application,
      communications, and participation in our programs and community.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Information we collect automatically.</strong> Technical and
      usage information about your device and how you interact with our
      website, collected through privacy-friendly, cookieless analytics.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How we use your information</h2>
  <p>We use personal information to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>assess applications and run our selection process;</li>
    <li>operate, administer, and deliver our programs and events;</li>
    <li>communicate with you and respond to your enquiries;</li>
    <li>understand and improve our website, programs, and communications;</li>
    <li>keep our community and events safe; and</li>
    <li>comply with our legal and regulatory obligations.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Our lawful bases for processing</h2>
  <p>
    Where the UK or EU GDPR applies, we rely on one or more of the following
    lawful bases when we process your personal information:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Consent:</strong> for example, for optional communications,
      non-essential cookies, and publishing certain information about you;
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Performance of a contract:</strong> to assess your application
      and to deliver the program to participants;
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Legitimate interests:</strong> to operate, secure, promote, and
      improve M3 and to communicate with our community, balanced against your
      rights and interests; and
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Legal obligation:</strong> to comply with applicable laws and
      regulatory requirements.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How we share your information</h2>
  <p>We share personal information in the following ways:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Constellation Institute.</strong> As our fiscal sponsor and
      operating partner, Constellation Institute processes personal information
      on our behalf and in its own right.
      <a href="https://constellation.org/privacy">Constellation Institute's Privacy Policy</a>
      applies to that processing.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Service providers and other third parties.</strong> We work with
      third parties who help us operate M3, our website, and our programs, and
      we may share personal information with them for those purposes. We may
      also share information with partner organisations we work with to deliver
      programs, including Constellation, Kairos and AISB, and with other
      third parties where appropriate. Some of these third parties may also
      process your information for their own purposes.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Publicity.</strong> We may publish information about our staff
      and participants (such as names, photos, professional affiliations, and
      testimonials) and photos or recordings from our events, on our website
      and social media. Where required, we ask for your consent first.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Legal and safety.</strong> We may share information where we
      believe it is necessary to comply with the law, enforce our terms, or
      protect the rights, property, or safety of M3, our participants, or
      others.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Business transfers.</strong> If M3 or its activities are
      reorganised or transferred, personal information may be transferred as
      part of that process.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>We do not sell your personal information.</p>

  <h2>Cookies and analytics</h2>
  <p>
    Any analytics we use are privacy-friendly and cookieless: they do not store
    cookies on your device or track you across other websites. This may include
    replaying how a visit moved through the page, with any typed input masked
    and IP addresses discarded. We may use your browser's local storage for
    essential features. We do not use advertising cookies.
  </p>

  <h2>How long we keep your information</h2>
  <p>
    We keep personal information only for as long as necessary for the purposes
    in this policy: for example, to maintain our alumni community and records,
    inform you of future programmes, and meet legal and record-keeping
    obligations (such as keeping financial records for the period required by
    law). We delete or anonymise information when we no longer need it, and you
    can ask us to delete your information at any time using the details below.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    Depending on where you live, you may have rights over your personal
    information, including the right to access, correct, delete, or restrict
    the processing of your information, to object to certain processing, and to
    data portability. Applicable data protection law, including the UK and EU
    GDPR, may apply to Constellation Institute's processing of your
    information. To
    exercise any of these rights, contact us using the details below. If you
    are in the UK or EEA, you also have the right to lodge a complaint with
    your local data protection authority (in the UK, the Information
    Commissioner's Office).
  </p>

  <h2>Keeping your information secure</h2>
  <p>
    We use appropriate technical and organisational measures to protect
    personal information, and limit access to those who need it. No method of
    transmission or storage is completely secure, so we cannot guarantee
    absolute security.
  </p>

  <h2>International transfers</h2>
  <p>
    We and our service providers may process personal information in countries
    other than your own. Where personal information is transferred
    internationally, we rely on appropriate safeguards as required by
    applicable law.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>
    M3 is intended for professionals aged 18 and over. We do not knowingly
    collect personal information from children.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this policy from time to time. When we do, we will revise the
    “last updated” date above and post the new version on this page.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact us</h2>
  <p>
    If you have any questions about this policy or how we handle your personal
    information, contact us at <a href="mailto:fernando@m3fellowship.com">fernando@m3fellowship.com</a>.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
